    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-31T04:10:39+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-31T04:10:39+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-30T18:40:39Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-30T18:40:39Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system southeast of SA continues extending a ridge across the state, as it moves over Victoria and into the Tasman Sea by late Monday. A cold front is then forecast to move across the state on Tuesday, as another ridge and high push in behind the front on Wednesday. Another cold front may slip across the southeast parts of SA early Thursday, with the high moving over eastern SA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-31T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 23 to 28.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower east of Ceduna in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h in the early morning then shifting south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Streaky Bay, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the evening. Light winds becoming northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending east to southeasterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 26.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
